The Sandbox stand-in (zzw-hackios-security-standins.patch of the stack) answered request 4, "container path of a
process", with success and an untouched buffer for a process that has no container (no CFFIXED_USER_HOME). The real
Sandbox fails the request there, and callers rely on it: SafariCore's
-[NSFileManager(SafariNSFileManagerExtras) _safari_getMobileSafariContainerDirectoryURL:isContainerized:] does
`if (sandbox_container_path_for_pid(getpid(), buf, 1024) == 0) url = [NSURL fileURLWithPath:@(buf) isDirectory:YES];`
else asks LaunchServices for MobileSafari's data container. With the success answer it built an NSString from the
uninitialized buffer, got nil and aborted ("-[NSURL initFileURLWithPath:isDirectory:]: nil string parameter") in
webbookmarksd, com.apple.Safari.History and Safari's DataMigrator plugin (DMLastMigrationResults success False on a
fresh Data). Now such a process gets ENOENT. Applies after zzw-hackios-security-standins.patch (name order).
diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_minimac.c b/bsd/kern/kern_minimac.c
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_minimac.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_minimac.c
@@ -142,8 +142,11 @@
  * extension -- has had the path from containermanagerd and passes it in the environment as
  * CFFIXED_USER_HOME, which is where Foundation takes the home directory from. So that is the
  * answer: it is looked up among the strings exec left at the top of the stack of the process.
- * A process without the variable has no container, and gets what every process got before:
- * success and an untouched buffer.
+ * A process without the variable has no container and gets ENOENT, as the Sandbox answers for
+ * a process that is not in one. (It used to get success and an untouched buffer: SafariCore's
+ * _safari_getMobileSafariContainerDirectoryURL:isContainerized: then took the buffer for its own
+ * container path, got nil and aborted, in webbookmarksd, com.apple.Safari.History and Safari's
+ * migration plugin, instead of asking LaunchServices for MobileSafari's data container.)
  */
 #define SANDBOX_SYSCALL_CONTAINER_PATH  4
 #define SANDBOX_CONTAINER_VARIABLE      "CFFIXED_USER_HOME="
@@ -187,7 +190,7 @@
 	task = proc_task(p);
 	if (user_stack == 0 || argslen == 0 || task == TASK_NULL) {
 		proc_rele(p);
-		return 0;
+		return ENOENT;
 	}
 	/* the same way as sysctl_procargsx(): the task keeps the map alive once the process is let go */
 	task_reference(task);
@@ -195,7 +198,7 @@
 	map = get_task_map_reference(task);
 	task_deallocate(task);
 	if (map == VM_MAP_NULL) {
-		return 0;
+		return ENOENT;
 	}
 	strings_size = vm_map_round_page(argslen, vm_map_page_mask(map));
 	if (kmem_alloc(kernel_map, &strings, strings_size, KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO, VM_KERN_MEMORY_BSD) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
@@ -211,10 +214,11 @@
 			vm_map_copy_discard(copy);
 		}
 		kmem_free(kernel_map, strings, strings_size);
-		return 0;                       /* the process is on its way out, or has unmapped its own stack */
+		return ENOENT;                       /* the process is on its way out, or has unmapped its own stack */
 	}
 
 	end = (const char *)(strings + strings_size);
+	error = ENOENT;                         /* no CFFIXED_USER_HOME: not in a container */
 	for (s = end - argslen; s < end; s += len + 1) {
 		len = strnlen(s, end - s);
 		if (len > prefix_len && s + len < end && strncmp(s, SANDBOX_CONTAINER_VARIABLE, prefix_len) == 0) {
